WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:07.040
From climbing on to leaving the machine: the basic steps from the Cat 320D manual.

00:00:07.040 --> 00:00:16.920
Face the machine when you get on or off, and keep three-point contact with the steps and handholds. Never mount or dismount a moving machine.

00:00:16.920 --> 00:00:26.120
Pull the belt out of the retractor in a continuous motion, fasten the catch into the buckle, and position the belt low across your lap.

00:00:26.120 --> 00:00:33.160
To release it, push the release button on the buckle. The belt retracts automatically.

00:00:33.160 --> 00:00:38.480
Before starting, turn the battery disconnect switch to the ON position.

00:00:38.480 --> 00:00:49.320
Move the hydraulic lockout control to LOCKED. The engine only starts with the lever in the LOCKED position. Then move the joysticks to HOLD.

00:00:49.320 --> 00:01:03.760
Make sure everyone is clear and briefly sound the horn. Turn the engine start switch to ON, set the engine speed dial to 1, then turn the switch to START and release the key once the engine starts.

00:01:03.760 --> 00:01:14.480
After working under load, stop the machine and run the engine at low idle for five minutes. Then turn the engine start switch to OFF and remove the key.

00:01:14.480 --> 00:01:25.240
If the engine does not stop, use the engine stop control below the left side of the operator seat: lift the cover and push the switch upward.

00:01:25.240 --> 00:01:37.840
Dismount facing the machine, using both hands on the steps and handholds. Then clean any debris out of the engine compartment and the front bottom guard to avoid a fire hazard.

00:01:37.840 --> 00:01:46.320
Finally, turn the battery disconnect switch to OFF. If you leave the machine for a month or longer, remove the key.
